<title>INDIA: INDIA M3 MONEY SUPPLY RISES TO 16.7 PCT ON JULY 18.</title>
<headline>INDIA M3 MONEY SUPPLY RISES TO 16.7 PCT ON JULY 18.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.7 percent on July 18, up from 16.3 percent on July 4, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   July 18, 1997  July 4, 1997   July 19, 1996</p>
<p>		   16.7	     16.3	     16.03</p>
<p>Money supply was 7,310.58 billion rupees on July 18 against 7,311.16 billion rupees on July 4 and 6,255.42 billion on July 19, 1996, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
